WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.899
One option if we hate our jobs obviously
is to leave it

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:04.140
but if we actually cannot 
leave our job for various reasons

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.826
the question is:

00:00:05.826 --> 00:00:08.670
What are we supposed to do?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.295
Be the leader you wish you had.

00:00:11.295 --> 00:00:15.360
Working at a hard job working for a bad boss

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.680
can sometimes be one of the greatest
educations ever.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.650
So the question is:

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.632
Can you change your mindset?

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:24.960
Instead of waking up in the morning going

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.140
"Oh I can't do this again"
but rather view it as university.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.863
You know, you're getting a master's degree in leadership

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.880
and you may be learning everything
how not to do things

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.400
and to wake up and be like, 
"What am I gonna learn today?"

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.260
Early on in my career I had a

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.190
really bad boss who believed that she
could get the most out of us by berating

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:41.690
us and she told me once that—I had
one of my "reviews"—and she said,

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.020
"You have no talent" 
and I was like "nothing?"

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.783
and she was like "nothing."

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:51.760
This was her way of, I guess, motivating me

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.039
but I had such a
good attitude about it for a couple of reasons.

00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:59.550
One, because I knew, I think knew, what I was up against every day

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.712
and instead of taking it personally

00:01:01.712 --> 00:01:04.739
I viewed it as as my education of how not to lead

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:05.239
and I literally would file this stuff
all the way and use it some day.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:09.340
I get to use it now.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.413
And also, misery loves company.

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:16.080
You know, I had fantastic a fantastic relationship with my team.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.689
We looked after each other because we all had this

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:20.286
the oppressive boss.

00:01:20.286 --> 00:01:24.119
We would compare the "advice" that we got in our

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:28.279
little career building sessions and
we took care of each other

00:01:28.279 --> 00:01:29.520
and so we had a responsibility to each other

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.299
and that's where we cut our teeth on being

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:35.229
leaders and it actually made the job
wonderful.

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:36.420
Yes there were days that were oppressive.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.870
Yes there were days that I hated.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.540
Yes, there were days I wanted to like, pull my hair out and just quit

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.476
but it's because of the team that I had

00:01:43.476 --> 00:01:45.649
and how we looked after each other

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:48.780
and the mindset of learning every day that I made the most of it.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.525
So I think mindset is a
huge huge huge part of

00:01:52.525 --> 00:01:57.100
actually getting some joy out of a difficult job.

